==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*unnaną}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term/t|osx|unnan}}, Old High German {{term/t|goh|unnan}}, Middle Dutch {{term/t|dum|onnen}} (Dutch {{term/t|nl|gunnen}}), Old Norse {{term/t|non|unna}} (Swedish {{term/t|sv|unna}}, Danish {{term/t|da|unde}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈunːɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to [[grant]] or [[bestow]] (+ ''dat'' (person) + ''gen'' (thing))
# to [[wish]]
# to [[intercede]]

====Conjugation====
{{ang-conj|type=pretpres|unnan|unnanne|ann|*anst|ann|unnon|unne|unnen|ūþe|ūþest|ūþe|ūþon|ūþe|ūþen|*unne|*unnaþ|unnende|unnen}}

====Descendants====
* Middle English: [[unne]]

